<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-09-02T12:51:49Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Police exhume body of former Czechoslovak foreign minister Jan Masaryk</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b95aeca465587d0eb2fe4e9fa140b2eabd86e3f33fad774beae7901f4316cd8a</id><updated>2026-09-02T12:51:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T12:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/police-exhume-body-of-former-czechoslovak-foreign-minister-jan-masaryk/a-78745254--691899c25c64.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/police-exhume-body-of-former-czechoslovak-foreign-minister-jan-masaryk/a-78745254?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The top diplomat was found dead on March 10, 1948, in the courtyard beneath his bathroom window, supposedly after a fall. Police said their probe aims to settle questions that have surrounded the death ever since.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Armed men abduct Kenyan editor, employer suspects government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5baa2b19450cbe553c3e79b65649c2e0180933cc745542d2d09e80bc36cfbb45</id><updated>2026-09-02T12:51:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T12:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/armed-men-abduct-kenyan-editor-employer-suspects-government/a-78721264--ff71d6e16ceb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/armed-men-abduct-kenyan-editor-employer-suspects-government/a-78721264?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A newspaper editor in Kenya was kidnapped from a car late on Tuesday and then located near a dam far away a few hours later. The Standard paper said it suspected state involvement in an attempt to intimidate reporters.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU summons Russian envoy over failed Leipzig drone attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ff217872463f76262434c9c1671f0e160016e2dbaf2b384cff387a477f3cf074</id><updated>2026-09-02T12:51:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T08:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-summons-russian-envoy-over-failed-leipzig-drone-attack/a-78687280--165732ae8dab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-summons-russian-envoy-over-failed-leipzig-drone-attack/a-78687280?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU's foreign policy chief Kaja Kallas said the attempted attack had "all the hallmarks of state-sponsored terrorism." She said the EU was summoning a Russian envoy, with France announcing a similar step.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>What really helps Europe deal with drought</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5c02e8af7e620b1be5399775a23f7ed201e96827cb04f090faae5d6dc43f7501</id><updated>2026-09-02T12:51:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T07:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-really-helps-europe-deal-with-drought/a-78577712--d183cadee76b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-really-helps-europe-deal-with-drought/a-78577712?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Fix leaks, or ban pools? As European countries prepare for hotter, drier years to come, here's what the data says about how to really save water</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>Charlie Kirk murder suspect to face potential death penalty</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3b442a8a318e019a8f21eb695f9e4d6ca9c6a64f21a2fa783f60333ddad82ef8</id><updated>2026-09-02T12:51:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T07:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/charlie-kirk-murder-suspect-to-face-potential-death-penalty/a-78664853--729208e5b5a4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/charlie-kirk-murder-suspect-to-face-potential-death-penalty/a-78664853?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Tyler R., accused of fatally shooting Charlie Kirk, will stand trial on aggravated murder charges after a Utah judge ruled prosecutors had enough evidence to seek the death penalty.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Women's football: Anyomi, London City and the German exodus</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ea2f535d65c3bcefd721a3d17b759a32beb2c4fbff732990fff56bec23a1a3f9</id><updated>2026-09-02T12:51:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T07:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/women-s-football-anyomi-london-city-and-the-german-exodus/a-78446131--26908c4ff9f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/women-s-football-anyomi-london-city-and-the-german-exodus/a-78446131?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nicole Anyomi has joined Alexia Putellas and other star names in signing for the ambitious English club London City Lionesses. The Germany winger told DW England is a better place to develop her game than back home.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Cargo ship with 10 crew sinks off Turkey coast — authorities</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d686d483416aa46db457e376292ba19987757fc2dc017138fc05a5d68b126f3d</id><updated>2026-09-02T12:51:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T06:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cargo-ship-with-10-crew-sinks-off-turkey-coast-authorities/a-78676617--bf06eae0d768.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cargo-ship-with-10-crew-sinks-off-turkey-coast-authorities/a-78676617?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Coast guard vessels and a helicopter are searching for 10 missing crew members off the coast of Istanbul. Authorities say they lost contact after the bulk carrier crashed into a chemical tanker off the coast of Istanbul.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Police probe suspected power station attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da14d754f07ba9f518c8d627c4f162d2c460631b3afc729d244baf22a2d360aa</id><updated>2026-09-02T12:51:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T06:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-police-probe-suspected-power-station-attacks/live-78669282--da9f01e1de4b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-police-probe-suspected-power-station-attacks/live-78669282?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police are investigating after homemade projectiles were used to damage power lines in eastern Germany. This comes amid suspicion of sabotage at another power station in the west of the country. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Tunisia's human rights defenders decry civil society crackdown</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e37dc2e76c92c5a5797b17ea748593fccf3657581537365b8c7cdac4a14ccbf8</id><updated>2026-09-02T12:50:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T04:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tunisia-s-human-rights-defenders-decry-civil-society-crackdown/a-78614966--0d15ca52876a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tunisia-s-human-rights-defenders-decry-civil-society-crackdown/a-78614966?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Five years into the authoritarian rule of Tunisian President Kais Saied, Human Rights Watch and other activists warn that Tunisia's once vibrant civil society is in danger of being completely stifled.</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry><entry><title>Hong Kong activist Joshua Wong pleads guilty to collusion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a3671817d9a44a85a873ccffde86047e1d493e75041d5816b6d2302661479ba5</id><updated>2026-09-02T12:50:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T02:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hong-kong-activist-joshua-wong-pleads-guilty-to-collusion/a-78657525--e463876939eb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hong-kong-activist-joshua-wong-pleads-guilty-to-collusion/a-78657525?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The prominent activist pleaded guilty to colluding with foreign entities. He faces a lengthy prison sentence.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran war: US, Tehran trade fire in new flare-up</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0630bf1c656ae8cf53716c0d62f9940f43cd5e1057d91b3ca269ae1d9c786c68</id><updated>2026-09-02T12:50:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T01:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-war-us-tehran-trade-fire-in-new-flare-up/live-78656656--b10423fe5e8c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-war-us-tehran-trade-fire-in-new-flare-up/live-78656656?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Explosions have been reported around the Strait of Hormuz, including at an airport in southern Iran. US President Donald Trump said the strikes were a response to Iranian attempts to mine the strait. Follow DW.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Russia threatens 'devastating' Baltic response</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:86294f9d264dff05e1e4735d59be712c506ba367950b33aad92d66ea94879112</id><updated>2026-09-02T12:50:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T00:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-threatens-devastating-baltic-response/live-78582421--7e6d420347ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-threatens-devastating-baltic-response/live-78582421?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Any escalation in the Baltic region will lead to a significant response, Moscow said.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany says Russia behind attempted drone attack at Leipzig airport</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d2010330e0c5eaa3fdc93ef1baaf0838f92d7832e9bb14a832645e8e5a870d0f</id><updated>2026-09-02T12:50:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T22:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-says-russia-behind-attempted-drone-attack-at-leipzig-airport/a-78584589--e12594bca2c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-says-russia-behind-attempted-drone-attack-at-leipzig-airport/a-78584589?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Investigators believe an explosives-laden drone was deliberately targeting a Ukrainian cargo aircraft at Leipzig/Halle airport in early August. The German government said on Tuesday that it held Russia "responsible."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran: US launches fresh strikes as hostilities flare again</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b9427b4259ed39cf5196fe735b1e9c03ce65dc81c782e34c308eef26941ba5d0</id><updated>2026-09-02T12:50:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T18:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-us-launches-fresh-strikes-as-hostilities-flare-again/a-78655364--98c85ec79ea8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-us-launches-fresh-strikes-as-hostilities-flare-again/a-78655364?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Explosions were reported in and around the Strait of Hormuz, as well as at an airport in southern Iran. US President Trump described the strikes as "large and powerful." Iran said the US will "regret" its latest attacks.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Congo's Ebola caseload tops 6,000 as concerns grow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c4993df95a376d0b8c5c20b270fac4f3bcb8baa1ee473a35a79128515db431a6</id><updated>2026-09-02T12:50:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T18:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/congo-s-ebola-caseload-tops-6-000-as-concerns-grow/a-78638447--f90029a93fe3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/congo-s-ebola-caseload-tops-6-000-as-concerns-grow/a-78638447?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of Congo has surpassed 6,000 confirmed cases, with nearly 3,000 deaths. As the virus spreads, authorities are racing to contain one of the deadliest outbreaks in history.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany terminates lease for Berlin's Russian House</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01d1c365839dfec53ba911308f3e5d88eaaa55a90f82858b519be480e227c925</id><updated>2026-09-02T12:50:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T16:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-terminates-lease-for-berlin-s-russian-house/a-73037945--51d0280fff89.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-terminates-lease-for-berlin-s-russian-house/a-73037945?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany has announced the termination of the lease for the Russian House in the heart of Berlin. Critics have long said it is a hub for propaganda and espionage.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Iran fuel crisis deepens amid war and sanctions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:41ddfff9cc401177753680930ffe8cb017fbdca63e5794990647635644cec0b7</id><updated>2026-09-02T12:51:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T14:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-fuel-crisis-deepens-amid-war-and-sanctions/a-78636429--e0c5fd131866.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-fuel-crisis-deepens-amid-war-and-sanctions/a-78636429?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Long lines at fuel stations are spreading across Iran as war damage, import constraints and new US sanctions squeeze supplies.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>As glaciers melt, can communities be protected?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:140b5c9b679e4a5cc3a7475df679320ba9dd8b8607cfe9a71873408d05042fbf</id><updated>2026-09-02T12:50:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T13:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-glaciers-melt-can-communities-be-protected/a-78615775--e5540929272d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/as-glaciers-melt-can-communities-be-protected/a-78615775?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rising temperatures are increasing the risk of floods and avalanches in mountain regions. The disaster in Nepal and Tibet shows the urgent need for solutions, and the tools that could help save lives.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Mladic's death, Bosnia and Serbia's unfinished reckoning</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b707311b17a3cae23ed3995fa8922aa026b073c50fdfc1ea277e0d5d390f9321</id><updated>2026-09-02T12:50:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T13:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/mladic-s-death-bosnia-and-serbia-s-unfinished-reckoning/a-78602733--5a8297f9dc8f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/mladic-s-death-bosnia-and-serbia-s-unfinished-reckoning/a-78602733?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The death of Ratko Mladic did not close a dark chapter of European history; it reopened old wounds. The ideology that created him lives on. The Dayton peace agreement ended the war, not the divisions that produced it.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Will Bangladesh join the Mecca defense alliance?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a91d62cd4c3c9b5ed255b7b433b422099aff5c8e09ba8e2f91b27864617a385f</id><updated>2026-09-02T12:50:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T12:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-bangladesh-join-the-mecca-defense-alliance/a-78613944--d550ab622814.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-bangladesh-join-the-mecca-defense-alliance/a-78613944?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">While Bangladesh weighs the risks of signing the Mecca Joint Defense Agreement, experts warn that such a move could complicate relations with neighboring India.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Norway's new King Haakon VIII takes oath in parliament</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:221464cce13dafb5f3f4cc6064dbbe380fc4e9e898b90e340570da5f1be1a339</id><updated>2026-09-02T12:50:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T12:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/norway-s-new-king-haakon-viii-takes-oath-in-parliament/a-78606923--cfde85175591.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/norway-s-new-king-haakon-viii-takes-oath-in-parliament/a-78606923?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The new king swore to uphold the constitution in parliament in Oslo, the first major institutional step of his reign. Haakon VIII's wife Queen Mette-Marit had to skip the event in the aftermath of her lung transplant.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
